# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose
#   Document environment variables required to run local integrations safely.
# Why this file exists
#   API tokens and model configuration must stay outside source code and Git.
# Responsibility
#   Provide example variable names and safe setup hints only; never place a real
#   token, password, or personal setting in this file.
# Implement later
#   Add only variables that the current code actually reads, likely GITHUB_TOKEN
#   and one model-provider key. Copy this file to `.env` locally when needed.
# Interacts with
#   `github_client.py` and `agent.py` will read configuration after you decide on
#   a small configuration approach. `.env` itself should be ignored by Git.
# Inputs and outputs
#   Input is values supplied by the developer; output is process environment
#   configuration available to the application.
# Concepts to practice
#   Environment variables, secrets management, `.gitignore`, and configuration
#   boundaries.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# MODEL_API_KEY=
